<title>USA: Nike wins patent suit against Wal-Mart.</title>
<headline>Nike wins patent suit against Wal-Mart.</headline>
<dateline>BEAVERTON, Ore. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nike Inc said Thursday a court has ordered Wal-Mart Stores Inc and its supplier  Hawe Yue Inc to pay the company $6 million in a patent infringement suit.</p>
<p>Nike said the U.S. District Court for the Eastern District of Virginia ordered Wal-Mart and Hawe Yue to pay Nike for infringement of the patented design of its Air Mada outdoor shoe.</p>
<p>Nike said in a statement that the court also prohibiting Wal-Mart and its supplier from selling any more infringing shoes. Nike said the case &quot;illustrates the actions Nike will take to protect the creative efforts of its designers and developers.&quot;</p>
</text>
